00:06:32,660 --> 00:06:34,900
With all the sound and fury of power saws,

107
00:06:34,901 --> 00:06:38,420
it's easy to miss some of the subtleties of what makes a saw a saw.

108
00:06:39,320 --> 00:06:41,780
For that, it helps to take a look at a simpler saw.

109
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:47,440
The panel saw, also known as a hand saw.

110
00:06:48,540 --> 00:06:51,000
Of course, the defining feature of a saw is its teeth.

111
00:06:51,860 --> 00:06:56,060
It's got separately formed teeth that cut into the material

112
00:06:56,061 --> 00:07:02,340
and slice the fibers away so that it cuts very, very quickly through the material.

113
00:07:02,341 --> 00:07:08,100
Saw teeth are only sharp on the forward edge, the cutting edge.

114
00:07:08,101 --> 00:07:11,580
They're also raked, inclined in the direction of the cut.

115
00:07:11,581 --> 00:07:17,460
On all western hand saws, the teeth all basically point in the same direction forward.

116
00:07:17,461 --> 00:07:20,900
That's because these saws are designed to cut on the push stroke.

117
00:07:20,901 --> 00:07:25,100
And when you pull the blade back, the saw isn't cutting.

118
00:07:25,101 --> 00:07:27,840
And for every tooth, there is a gullet.

119
00:07:27,841 --> 00:07:34,340
The gullets are the spaces between the teeth, and these spaces are allowed to fill up with

120
00:07:34,341 --> 00:07:35,840
the material that's being cut away.

121
00:07:35,841 --> 00:07:37,080
It's called swarf.

122
00:07:37,081 --> 00:07:40,880
The swarf builds up in these little gullets, and then as soon as the blade exits at the

123
00:07:40,881 --> 00:07:44,740
bottom of the board, the swarf just falls out of the gullets and falls away.

124
00:07:44,741 --> 00:07:47,240
The last key feature is the kerf.

125
00:07:47,241 --> 00:07:51,320
The width of any saw cut is known as the kerf, and it's worth knowing this measurement to

126
00:07:51,321 --> 00:07:53,620
get the most accurate cut.

127
00:07:53,621 --> 00:07:58,900
The actual cutting edge creates a wider curve than the thickness of the blade, so the blade

128
00:07:58,901 --> 00:08:02,160
has clearance and doesn't stick in the curve.

129
00:08:02,161 --> 00:08:05,720
Despite all these design features, there's still plenty of skill involved in making a

130
00:08:05,721 --> 00:08:07,720
