156
00:10:04,261 --> 00:10:08,260
And naturally, they could only cut very, very soft woods.

157
00:10:08,261 --> 00:10:13,260
Then we basically progressed to a point where we use harder and harder materials,

158
00:10:13,261 --> 00:10:18,260
bronze and bronze alloys that have the ability to hold a little bit of a better edge,

159
00:10:18,261 --> 00:10:20,260
right up until we get to iron.

160
00:10:20,261 --> 00:10:24,260
And of course, iron is where we make a major leap into tools

161
00:10:24,261 --> 00:10:27,260
that were really capable of doing some pretty serious work,

162
00:10:27,261 --> 00:10:32,260
felling trees and, you know, cutting up very thick logs.

163
00:10:32,261 --> 00:10:41,200
The saws of the Iron Age, roughly 700 BC to 50 AD, incorporated two breakthroughs.

